  "body": "Stacked on #3900 (U1). The base is `main`, because #3900 is a fork branch. The diff of U2 alone: https://github.com/qsmits/Camcraft/compare/be7168455...issue/3893-tool-library-editor\n\n## What changed\n\nU2 of #3663: you edit a tool in the tool library window.\n\n- A tool opens in the window's editor. The list folds into a rail on the left (\"All tools\" and one row for each tool).\n- The editor has two tabs:\n  - **Tool**: the type, the geometry and the kind rows. The tab calls `tool_settings_grid::geometry` (with `kind_rows`). It does not copy them.\n  - **Details**: the material group, the catalog facts of #898 and the tool number. The tab calls `tool_settings_grid::catalog` (with `tool_catalog_rows::catalog_rows`).\n- **Apply** queues the same commands as the Apply of Properties: `State::apply_tool_numbers` (`ChangeTool`, or `ReshapeTool` when a drawn cutter rides the change) and `push_number_if_changed` (`SetToolNumber`, only when the number changed). A geometry and catalog edit is one undo step.\n- **Edit tool shape** opens the existing shape window. That window edits through the draft of Properties. Thus, when Properties shows a different tool, Properties first moves to the tool of the window.\n- The window keeps its **own draft** (`ToolLibraryView::editor`). Properties keeps `State::tool_ui`. `State::with_library_draft` swaps the draft of the window (and its sync key) into `tool_ui` only while the window draws and applies. Each draft has its own `(name, doc_version)` key, so typing in one draft never resets the other.\n- The \"Edit\" button of the Document list opens the tool in the window. A new window opens on the tool that Properties shows. A pick in the window does not change the selection or the subject of Properties.\n- If the open tool goes out of the document, the editor closes and the full list shows again.\n- Decision: `docs/decisions/3893-tool-library-editor.md`.\n\nNo new command. No MCP tool is owed. Properties keeps all its groups. The holder, the cutting data and the drawing come to the window in U3 to U5.\n\n## Readings\n\n- `crates/ui` lib: 1,595 passed, 0 failed, 8 ignored. The `#[test]` count goes up by 4. No test was removed or ignored.\n- No snapshot PNG changed. No `Cargo.toml` or `Cargo.lock` changed. Each new file has fewer than 170 lines.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `egui_app::tests::tool_library_editor::apply_is_one_change_tool_and_undo_restores`\n- `egui_app::tests::tool_library_editor::the_dialog_draft_and_the_properties_draft_do_not_mix`\n- `egui_app::tests::tool_library_editor::details_tab_shows_the_catalog_facts`\n- `egui_app::tests::page_layout_tool_library::layout_window_tool_editor`\n\n## Gate (Windows, winbuild, trial merge of head bae9b7b5a with origin/main 1e182f2cf)\n\n- Targeted: the four pinning tests and `layout_window_tool_library`: pass.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: 18 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled, wall time 5.2 min. The steps were the ui build, `ui suites: lib` and 16 ui suites (boundary, boundary_picks, catalog_render, contour_dxf_sketch, feedback, fixtures, gpu_render, machine, models, operations, shell, sinker_setup, tap_hand, theme_example, theme_files, waterjet_tool).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: pass.\n- No post, toolpath or geometry changed. Thus no `example_catalog*` suite is necessary, and the light lane reaches no step.\n- An earlier gate run on head 5c7c79cd0 failed on a wrong import path in the new test file (`egui_kittest::Node`). The fix is commit 407680617.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- A real typing session in the running app. The tests set the drafts directly and click Apply, Details and the rail through AccessKit.\n- The shape window opened from the editor, while Properties shows a different tool. The code path is short, but no test pins it.\n- macOS and Linux builds.\n\n## Screenshots\n\nRendered without a window with egui_kittest, from a scratch test that is not committed.\n\n| | Before (U1 head be7168455) | After (this PR) |\n|---|---|---|\n| Window open | ![before list](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/pr-3893/before-1-list.png) | ![after list](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/pr-3893/after-1-list.png) |\n| \"Edit\" on a tool | ![before edit](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/pr-3893/before-2-edit.png) | ![after edit](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/pr-3893/after-2-edit.png) |\n| Details tab | - | ![after details](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/pr-3893/after-3-details.png) |\n\nChangelog: Edit a tool's geometry and catalog facts in the tool library window. Apply is one undo step.\n\nEffort: high (the issue has no labels; the plan says effort:high).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\nFixes #3893\n",
